type=\"image.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"567\" height=\"567\" src=\"https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/10\/Chhem_rethy.jpg\" class=\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-12681\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/10\/Chhem_rethy.jpg 567w, https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/10\/Chhem_rethy-300x300.jpg 300w, https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/10\/Chhem_rethy-150x150.jpg 150w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 567px) 100vw, 567px\" \/>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-398088c elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\" data-id=\"398088c\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"heading.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t<h6 class=\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\">Dr. Rethy Chhem<\/h6>\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-44e6484 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"44e6484\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p>Distinguished Professor of Technology and Humanities<\/p>\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-column elementor-col-50 elementor-top-column elementor-element elementor-element-d860074\" data-id=\"d860074\" data-element_type=\"column\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-698831e elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"698831e\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p>Professor Chhem Kieth Rethy is currently Senior Minister and Distinguished Professor of AI and Humanities at CamTech University, Cambodia. His academic work bridges artificial intelligence, humanities, philosophy of technology, ethics, and global governance.<\/p>\n\n<p>He holds a medical degree (MD) and two PhDs, in History and in Education, reflecting a rare interdisciplinary formation that informs his work across science, humanities, and policy.<\/p>\n\n<p>He teaches Introduction to the Humanities at the undergraduate level and supervises PhD students in technology governance, technology management, and AI, focusing on ethical leadership, responsible innovation, and global AI governance. He also leads the Center for Buddhist AI Ethics, advancing research on compassion-based approaches to AI and interdisciplinary dialogue on ethics and technology.<\/p>\n\n<p>Previously, he was a Professor of Radiology at McGill University, Western University, and the National University of Singapore. He also served as a senior United Nations diplomat and Director of the Division of Human Health at the International Atomic Energy Agency (IAEA).<\/p>\n\n<p>He is a laureate of the Dr. Nagai Memorial Peace Award, Japan (2025). He is also a Fellow of the Academy of Engineering and Technology of the Developing World.<\/p>\n\n<p>His career integrates medicine, education, history, science diplomacy, and AI ethics, contributing to interdisciplinary scholarship and policy engagement at the global level.<\/p>\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/section>\n\t\t\t\t<section class=\"elementor-section elementor-top-section elementor-element elementor-element-6d3f9c3 elementor-section-boxed elementor-section-gap-beside-yes elementor-section-height-default elementor-section-height-default elementor-section-column-vertical-align-stretch\" data-id=\"6d3f9c3\" data-element_type=\"section\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-container elementor-column-gap-extended\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-column elementor-col-100 elementor-top-column elementor-element elementor-element-660abd8\" data-id=\"660abd8\" data-element_type=\"column\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-b892d96 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_icon elementor-view-default elementor-widget-divider--element-align-center elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"b892d96\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n\t\t\t<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-icon elementor-divider__element\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"e-font-icon-svg e-fas-university\" viewBox=\"0 0 512 512\" xmlns=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/2000\/svg\"><path d=\"M496 128v16a8 8 0 0 1-8 8h-24v12c0 6.627-5.373 12-12 12H60c-6.627 0-12-5.373-12-12v-12H24a8 8 0 0 1-8-8v-16a8 8 0 0 1 4.941-7.392l232-88a7.996 7.996 0 0 1 6.118 0l232 88A8 8 0 0 1 496 128zm-24 304H40c-13.255 0-24 10.745-24 24v16a8 8 0 0 0 8 8h464a8 8 0 0 0 8-8v-16c0-13.255-10.745-24-24-24zM96 192v192H60c-6.627 0-12 5.373-12 12v20h416v-20c0-6.627-5.373-12-12-12h-36V192h-64v192h-64V192h-64v192h-64V192H96z\"><\/path><\/svg><\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/span>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/section>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>\u00ab Go back to Our People page Faculty members Dr. Rethy Chhem Distinguished Professor of Technology and Humanities Professor Chhem Kieth Rethy is currently Senior Minister and Distinguished Professor of AI and Humanities at CamTech University, Cambodia. His academic work bridges artificial intelligence, humanities, philosophy of technology, ethics, and global governance. He holds a medical degree (MD) and two PhDs, in History and in Education, reflecting a rare interdisciplinary formation that informs his work across science, humanities, and policy. He teaches Introduction to the Humanities at the undergraduate level and supervises PhD students in technology governance, technology management, and AI, focusing on ethical leadership, responsible innovation, and global AI governance. He also leads the Center for Buddhist AI Ethics, advancing research on compassion-based approaches to AI and interdisciplinary dialogue on ethics and technology. Previously, he was a Professor of Radiology at McGill University, Western University, and the National University of Singapore. He also served as a senior United Nations diplomat and Director of the Division of Human Health at the International Atomic Energy Agency (IAEA). He is a laureate of the Dr. Nagai Memorial Peace Award, Japan (2025). He is also a Fellow of the Academy of Engineering and Technology of the Developing World. His career integrates medicine, education, history, science diplomacy, and AI ethics, contributing to interdisciplinary scholarship and policy engagement at the global level.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":4,"featured_media":0,"parent":0,"menu_order":0,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","template":"elementor_header_footer","meta":{"_acf_changed":false,"footnotes":""},"class_list":["post-12676","page","type-page","status-publish","hentry","post-no-thumbnail"],"acf":[],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/12676","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/page"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/4"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=12676"}],"version-history":[{"count":5,"href":"https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/wp-json\/wp\/